course: dictionary
lesson: 10302
title: Tour: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «We went on a tour of the castle with a guide who explained everything.» The guide and the explaining tell you that a tour here is a walk around one place.
explain: «The band is on tour this summer, playing in ten cities.» Here tour means a trip where a band travels to perform in many places. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: "The band is travelling to perform in ten cities" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Tour can also be a verb, an action word. «We toured the old town on Saturday.» To tour means to travel around a place to see it. Look at the words around the word, and ask: is it a thing, or something someone is doing?
fact: A tour can be a trip visiting several places, a walk around one place with a guide, or a trip by a band, team or show to perform in many places.
fact: Tour is a noun (a tour, tours) and a verb (to tour, toured, touring).
fact: In maths, a tour may cost a set price per person. Price per person × number of people = total cost.
fact: «The Tour de France» is a famous cycling race held every July that finishes in Paris.
fact: In French, un tour means a trip, but une tour means a tower, like la tour Eiffel.
exercise: «We went on a guided tour of the school, and the guide told us about its history.» What does tour mean here? | *A walk around one place with a guide who explains things | A tower in Paris | Racing on bikes | A band performing in many cities
exercise: «The band is on tour this summer, playing in ten cities.» What does on tour mean? | Sleeping late | Lost on a mountain | *Travelling to perform in many places | Stuck in one place all summer
exercise: A bus tour costs £12 for each person. Four people go on the tour. What is the total cost? | £36 | £16 | *£48 | £12
test: «We toured the old town on Saturday.» What does toured mean? | Ran away from the town | Built a new house in the town | *Travelled around the town to see it | Painted the walls of the town
test: In French, une tour means what? | A book | A trip, like a school trip | *A tower, like la tour Eiffel | A pound of money
exam: «The Tour de France is a famous cycling race held every July that finishes in Paris.» In this name, what does tour suggest? | A guided walk around a museum | A swimming trip in a pool | *A race that travels through many places, ending in Paris | A tower in Paris
